### Sample 04 — retry, dead-letter and requeue
### The API runs on 5004; the shared receiver on 5100.

@api = http://localhost:5004
@receiver = http://localhost:5100

### The sample's index
GET {{api}}/

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Phase 1 — survivable failure. MaxAttempts is 4, so three rejections recover.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Clear the receiver first: DELETE also resets the failure budget.
DELETE {{receiver}}/deliveries

### Now set the budget.
POST {{receiver}}/fail-next/3

### Place an order. Copy the outboxId from the response into the requests below.
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "acme",
  "customerId": "cust-retry",
  "total": 42.00
}

### Inspect the record. Run it repeatedly to watch Failed -> Delivered and the
### attempt count climb. nextAttemptAt is when the dispatcher may try again.
GET {{api}}/outbox/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Four attempts, one record: distinctOutboxIds must be 1.
GET {{receiver}}/deliveries/summary

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Phase 2 — unsurvivable failure. More rejections than attempts.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

###
DELETE {{receiver}}/deliveries

###
POST {{receiver}}/fail-next/50

###
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "acme",
  "customerId": "cust-deadletter",
  "total": 42.00
}

### The operator's queue. LastError says why each record is here.
GET {{api}}/outbox/dead-lettered

### Aggregate counters, which the health check is built on.
GET {{api}}/outbox/stats

### Degraded while a dead letter exists - but still HTTP 200, because the
### service itself is working.
GET {{api}}/health/outbox

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Phase 3 — recovery.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Clears the forced-failure budget, so this time the receiver accepts.
DELETE {{receiver}}/deliveries

### Replay it. Both identifiers are preserved, so the replay is idempotent for a
### consumer that deduplicates. Returns 409 if the record is not dead-lettered.
POST {{api}}/outbox/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000/requeue

### Delivered, with the original outboxId and eventId, attemptCount back at 1.
GET {{api}}/outbox/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Empty again.
GET {{api}}/outbox/dead-lettered
